# =============================================================================
# OpenAD monorepo — environment layout
# =============================================================================
# Loader: `scripts/with-monorepo-env.sh`
#
#   • docker (alias: root) → `docker/.env` + `docker/.env.<dev|test|prod>`
#        Only for: `pnpm docker:*`, `minio:init-media-bucket`, other host
#        commands that need compose ports / broker bootstrap creds / MinIO.
#        Never load these files into Angular or Capacitor builds.
#
#   • app <folder> → repo root `.env` + `.env.<suffix>` + `app/<folder>/.env*`
#        Root layer must stay NON-SECRET: public URLs, log level, feature flags
#        that are safe in web/tablet bundles. Put JWT, DB, MQTT client secrets,
#        S3 keys, etc. in `app/<name>/.env*` only.
#
# Later files win (`--overload`). Encrypt with dotenvx from repo root; use `-fk .env.keys`.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A. Repo root — public / shareable (optional `.env` + `.env.dev` …)
#    Loaded by: `with-monorepo-env.sh app …` ONLY (not by Docker commands).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# API origin for tablet/ad-client builds (`tablet-env.token.ts`) and tooling
# API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1
# Admin SPA / marketing / deep links (document for teams; wire in Angular if needed)
# PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000
# MANAGEMENT_APP_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4200
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# B. docker/ — Docker Compose + MinIO host scripts ONLY
#    Files: `docker/.env`, `docker/.env.dev`, …   Template: `docker/.env.example`
#    Loaded by: `with-monorepo-env.sh docker -- …`
#
#    pnpm docker:reset — tear down & recreate containers (picks up compose/env changes).
#    pnpm docker:reset:volumes — same + delete named volumes (Mongo/Rabbit/Redis/MinIO data;
#      use after changing MONGO_INITDB_* or other first-boot-only settings).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- docker-compose.yml ---
# MINIO_API_PORT=9000
# MINIO_CONSOLE_PORT=9001
# MQTT_PORT=1884
# MQTT_AMQP_PORT=5672
# MQTT_MANAGEMENT_PORT=15672
# MQTT_MANAGEMENT_USER=openad
# MQTT_MANAGEMENT_PASSWORD=openad-dev-mqtt
# MONGO_INITDB_ROOT_USERNAME=openad
# MONGO_INITDB_ROOT_PASSWORD=openad-dev-mongo

# --- Host scripts (MinIO bucket init, aws CLI) ---
# S3_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9000
# MINIO_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9000
# S3_BUCKET=openad-media
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=minioadmin
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=minioadmin
# S3_REGION=us-east-1

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# C. app/openad-api — Nest API (secrets + service config)
#    Files: `app/openad-api/.env`, `app/openad-api/.env.dev`, …
#    Loaded after repo root public layer: `with-monorepo-env.sh app openad-api -- …`
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Core (typical boot) ---
# Root user lives in `admin`; app DB is `openad` (must match docker MONGO_INITDB_* password).
# MONGO_URI=mongodb://openad:openad-dev-mongo@127.0.0.1:27017/openad?authSource=admin
# MONGOOSE_AUTO_INDEX=false   # optional: disable automatic index builds from schemas (default: on)
# REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6379
# JWT_SECRET=change-me-access-secret
# JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=change-me-refresh-secret
# PORT=3000

# --- MQTT client (API subscribes/publishes; creds often match broker default user) ---
# MQTT_URL=mqtt://openad:openad-dev-mqtt@127.0.0.1:1884
# Optional: split creds out of URL
# MQTT_USERNAME=
# MQTT_PASSWORD=
# Optional TLS file paths:
# MQTT_TLS_CA=
# MQTT_TLS_CERT=
# MQTT_TLS_KEY=

# --- RabbitMQ Management HTTP API (health, pairing tablet users, api:seed MQTT ACL) ---
# Same names as broker admin; must NOT be loaded into frontends (keep in this file only).
# MQTT_MANAGEMENT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:15672
# MQTT_MANAGEMENT_USER=openad
# MQTT_MANAGEMENT_PASSWORD=openad-dev-mqtt
# MQTT_HEALTH_DISABLED=false
# MQTT_HEALTH=rabbitmq   # rabbitmq | http | none
# MQTT_HTTP_CHECK_URL=   # when MQTT_HEALTH=http
# RABBITMQ_PROVISION_DEVICE_MQTT_USERS=true
# RABBITMQ_SEED_API_MQTT_USER=true   # false = skip api:seed broker step. If MQTT_URL user equals
# MQTT_MANAGEMENT_USER, seed skips management HTTP calls (Docker default user already has full access).
# RABBITMQ_MQTT_VHOST=/
# RABBITMQ_MQTT_EXCHANGE=amq.topic
# RABBITMQ_TABLET_CLASSIC_CONFIGURE_REGEX=^mqtt-subscription-.*$
# RABBITMQ_TABLET_CLASSIC_WRITE_REGEX=^(amq\.topic|mqtt-subscription-.*)$
# RABBITMQ_TABLET_CLASSIC_READ_REGEX=^(amq\.topic|mqtt-subscription-.*)$
# Legacy shared tablet MQTT user when provisioning is off:
# MQTT_DEVICE_USER=
# MQTT_DEVICE_PASS=

# --- S3-compatible object storage (Cloudflare R2, AWS S3, MinIO) ---
# Single engine: `AssetStorageService` + optional `S3StorageService` (media) use the same client.
# Local dev MinIO: S3_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9000, S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true, keys match MINIO_ROOT_* in docker-compose.
# R2: use S3_REGION=auto and S3_ENDPOINT=https://<ACCOUNT_ID>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# S3_REGION=auto
# S3_BUCKET=openad-media
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# S3_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9000
# S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true
# Jest: `createTestApp()` overrides AssetStorageService with an in-memory implementation (no bucket calls).

# --- Public URLs & signing (presigned assets, command payloads, pairing MQTT host) ---
# Prefer repo root PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL for non-secret origin; override here if needed.
# PUBLIC_ASSET_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000
# PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000
# ASSET_URL_SIGNING_SECRET=change-me-asset-url-signing-secret

# --- Ephemeral object cleanup (S3) ---
# REPORT_EXPORT_RETENTION_DAYS=30
# SCREENSHOT_RETENTION_DAYS=14

# --- Releases / MDM APK distribution (009) ---
# Uses `PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` (see repo root section A) to build absolute URLs in manifests.
# S3 key prefix for APK objects (stored via AssetStorageService). Default: releases/apk
# RELEASE_APK_OBJECT_PREFIX=releases/apk

# --- Pairing & device behaviour ---
# PAIRING_SECRET_TTL_MS=600000
# SKIP_ASSET_ROTATION=false

# --- Optional admin bootstrap (`pnpm api:seed` also reads these) ---
# SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL=
# SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Media resolution, duration, file size, fleet health, analytics, and fraud thresholds are
# NOT configured via env. Use the admin app: Settings → Platform (Mongo-backed platform_config).

# --- Media VFS (007 — presigned direct-to-storage uploads) ---
# MEDIA_VFS_TENANT_KEY_PREFIX=openad
# MEDIA_UPLOAD_SESSION_TTL_SECONDS=3600
# MEDIA_ALLOWED_MIME_TYPES=video/mp4,image/jpeg,image/png
# DOOH_RULESET_VERSION=2026.1
# MEDIA_VFS_DEDUP=false

# --- Power thresholds (env; not on platform UI) ---
# POWER_ENGINE_OFF_VOLTAGE_V=12
# POWER_ENGINE_OFF_GRACE_MS=30000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# D. app/openad-management — Admin web (Angular)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build/serve inlines these via @ngx-env/builder (see app/openad-management/project.json ngxEnv.prefix).
# API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1
# PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# E. app/openad-ad-client — Tablet (Capacitor) build-time env
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Loaded via @ngx-env/builder (see app/openad-ad-client/project.json ngxEnv.prefix).
# Keep this layer non-secret: URLs and timing only. Tablet MQTT credentials are never
# hard-coded in env — each device receives broker username/password from pairing bind.

# API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1
# POWER_ENGINE_OFF_GRACE_MS=30000

# MQTT_URL — broker base URL only (e.g. mqtt://127.0.0.1:1884 or wss://… for web dev).
# Fallback when the bind response does not include mqtt.brokerUrl; pairing still supplies credentials.
# Do not set MQTT_USERNAME / MQTT_PASSWORD for production tablets (not used once paired).

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# F. Tests
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# See `.env.test.example` and `app/openad-api/.env.test` if you use file-based overrides.
